    cards: [
      { id: 'cb075-constraint-completeness', term: 'Constraint completeness review', kind: 'checklist', tool_scope: 'reasoning-only', match: ['sdc', 'timing constraints', '타이밍 제약', '합성 제약', 'create_clock', 'unconstrained path'], source_ids: ['openroad-docs'], summary: 'Before reading slack, check that every clock source and generated clock is defined with the right period and relationship, input and output delays exist for all ports, clock uncertainty and transition limits are set, and every false or multicycle path exception has a written reason. Unconstrained endpoints report no violation because nothing is checked. A suspiciously clean run is often a constraint gap.' },
      { id: 'cb075-qor-delta', term: 'QoR delta attribution', kind: 'calculation', tool_scope: 'calculation', match: ['qor', 'area increase', '면적 증가', '합성 결과', 'wns', 'tns'], source_ids: ['yosys-docs', 'openroad-docs'], summary: 'Compare runs metric by metric: total area and area by cell class (sequential, combinational, buffers, macros), worst and total negative slack, failing endpoint count, and flop count. A jump in buffers suggests timing pressure or high fanout; a change in flop count suggests RTL or retiming changes. Change one variable per experiment when possible, and mark any delta whose cause is not supported by evidence as unexplained.' },
      { id: 'cb075-warning-triage', term: 'Synthesis warning triage', kind: 'failure-mode', tool_scope: 'reasoning-only', match: ['synthesis warning', 'latch', '합성 경고', '상수 전파', 'removed register', 'multiple drivers'], source_ids: ['yosys-docs'], summary: 'Some warnings signal real bugs: inferred latches, multiple drivers, registers removed because they are constant or unloaded (often a missing connection), width mismatches, and black-boxed modules that should have been synthesised. Group warnings by type and count, review every instance of the dangerous types, and do not dismiss a whole category because most instances are benign.' },
      { id: 'cb075-optimisation-tradeoffs', term: 'Optimisation trade-off settings', kind: 'method', tool_scope: 'reasoning-only', match: ['retiming', 'clock gating', '리타이밍', '클럭 게이팅', 'flatten', 'logic optimization'], source_ids: ['yosys-docs', 'skywater-pdk'], summary: 'Retiming moves registers to balance logic but breaks register-name mapping for equivalence checks and debug. Flattening enables cross-boundary optimisation but loses hierarchy for later analysis. Clock gating saves dynamic power but adds gating cells and timing checks. Record each enabled option, why it was chosen, and what downstream step (equivalence, DFT, STA) must account for it.' },
      { id: 'cb075-prelayout-realism', term: 'Pre-layout timing realism', kind: 'stop-condition', tool_scope: 'reasoning-only', match: ['wire load', 'pre-layout timing', '배치 전 타이밍', '배선 지연', 'placement aware', 'timing margin'], source_ids: ['openroad-docs', 'skywater-pdk'], summary: 'Synthesis timing estimates interconnect delay without real placement. If the design has long cross-chip paths, large fanout or congested regions, post-layout slack can be much worse. Keep a margin on pre-layout slack and flag paths that cross block or macro boundaries. If worst slack at synthesis is already near zero, stop and address architecture or constraints before handing to physical design.' },
      { id: 'cb075-library-boundary', term: 'Library and tool boundary', kind: 'boundary', tool_scope: 'reasoning-only', match: ['liberty', 'standard cell library', '표준 셀 라이브러리', '공정 코너', 'pvt corner', 'vendor tool'], source_ids: ['skywater-pdk', 'yosys-docs'], summary: 'Results depend on the standard-cell library and the process, voltage and temperature corner used. An open PDK such as SKY130 can illustrate the flow but its numbers do not transfer to a commercial node. State the library and corner behind every number. Vendor tool commands and options must be checked against that vendor\'s documentation; do not present them as verified here.' },
    ],
