    summary: 'Aligns learning outcomes, activities and assessment, judges the strength of evidence for an intervention, and designs fair, valid measurement of learning.',
    mission: 'Learning outcomes, instructional design and assessment.',
    questions: ['What should learners be able to do afterwards, and how will we observe it?', 'Is the evidence that this intervention improves learning strong, relevant to our learners, and about learning rather than satisfaction?', 'Does the assessment measure the intended skill fairly for all learners, and what decisions will its scores support?'],
